      "license": "CC BY 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0",
      "artist": "dave conner from Inverness, Scotland",
      "description": "Constable Simon MacDonald joined the force in May 1902 and was transerred that September to Fort William, and then in 1904 he moved again to Onich, south of Fort William. \nHe later moved to Foyers (1912) and was then posted to Cannich in 1913 where he remained until 1920 when moving to Stoneybrige on the Isle of South Uist for the remarkably brief period of a year before returning to Drumnadrochit - where he remained for 14 years till he retired on pension. \nHis grandson also subsequently served as beat officer at Cannich.\n\nDate and location of this photograph are uncertain but I suspect it was during his period at Onich, as this card was in the same bundle of papers as the 1906 \"Locheil Welcome Arch\" one.",
